  "scenes": [
    {"text": "It is smaller than a grain of rice, and it is the deadliest animal on Earth.", "durationSeconds": 4.5, "asset": "samples/mosquito-albimanus.jpg"},
    {"text": "In 2024, malaria infected an estimated 282 million people.", "durationSeconds": 4, "asset": "samples/mosquito-stephensi.jpg"},
    {"text": "It killed about 610,000 of them.", "durationSeconds": 3.2},
    {"text": "Ninety five percent of those deaths were in Africa.", "durationSeconds": 3.4},
    {"text": "And three in four of them were children under five.", "durationSeconds": 3.6},
    {"text": "It starts with a bite from a female Anopheles mosquito, which carries a parasite.", "durationSeconds": 4.5},
    {"text": "The parasite multiplies in the liver, then invades red blood cells.", "durationSeconds": 4.2},
    {"text": "For centuries, the cure came from tree bark: cinchona, and later quinine.", "durationSeconds": 4.4},
    {"text": "In 1972, Tu Youyou discovered artemisinin. In 2021, the first malaria vaccine was recommended.", "durationSeconds": 5.4},
    {"text": "The fight is not over, but it can be won.", "durationSeconds": 4.2}
  ],
